From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 01:09:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 16/19] Wire the paid month behind one command

Everything needed to turn API quota into estimates existed in pieces; this
puts them in the order that matters. The sweep caches every response, so an
interrupted run resumes without spending units again, and the acceptance test
runs before the fit rather than after: a seed it rejects is not fitted at all
unless the operator asks for that explicitly, which is the difference between
a cheap data source and a published number that is quietly wrong.

Day sampling is weekday-balanced rather than evenly spaced. Seven days spread
across thirty-one lands on a step of four and happens to work, but a step that
is a multiple of seven would hit the same weekday every time; stepping by a
number coprime with seven walks every weekday in turn. Carrier mix moves with
the weekly schedule, so over-representing a weekday biases the seed.

